In a recent ascension I was faced with two unidentified Amulets of
Yendor and no means of identification.  However, Rodney quickly showed
up, stole one of them, thus identifying it for me.  I immediately
dropped the remaining Amulet from my inventory picked up the real one
and went on to ascend.  Just as I hit the go upstairs button on level
one it hit me that I was not 100% sure that the Wizard would always
steal the real amulet causing a moment of panic.  Had he stolen the
fake one I would have just lost my game.   Of course, there are many
ways to identify the Amulet (for example I'm assuming that if I took
off for the exit with the fake amulet and left the real one on the
ground, Rodney would no longer bother me, causing some suspicion as to
the value of the so-called Amulet of Yendor I was carrying) besides
the obvious scrolls and spells of identify.  However, the spoiled-but-
not-too-spoiled players out there like me could fall victim to it on a
rare occasion.  Chalk up one more YASD (or YASE;  Yet Another Stupid
Escape).

